    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1:
 
Fully staffed and operational  Innovative finance lab

Output 2:

TA support provided to TAs on digital fintech
Seed funding provided to 15-20 MSMEs
Digital financial toolkit developed and trainings delivered 

Output 3: 
MPTF established/operational procedures defined 
7 national staffs maintained at CMPIT 

Output 4: 

I research on MSMEs inclusion in the capital markets concluded</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1:
No available staff for the IFL
Non-existent procedures and documents developed for the lab
Non-existent CDF in the innovative finance space 

Output 2:

Limited TA support to MSMEs
Limited availability of seed funding 
Lack of awareness on digital finance and no digital literacy toolkit developed 

Output 3:

No multi-donor trust fund to support CMPIT
No budget to cover staff salary for 7 national advisors at CMPIT

Output 4: 

No research on MSMEs inclusion in the capital market</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1 :

2 - 3 staffs deployed to run and manage the innovative finance lab 
1 Catalytic Debt Fund established 
One firm hired to manage the Technical Assistance Facility 
The lab will be launched on sept- October 2022

Output 2:
20 MSME/start ups supported with pre-post investment TA on digital fintechs
20 MSMEs provided with seed capital to pilot/scale up digital financial products 
15-20 MSMEs trained on financial inclusion and digital financial technologies

Output 3:
1 multi-donor trust fund established and a technical working group
Support to cover salary for 7 national staffs continued 

Output 4

1 research conducted on MSMEs inclusion in the capital market, covering structural issues</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
